## 0102-dxgi-composition-swapchain-and-getdc.patch  (subject: dxgi: CreateSwapChainForComposition and a working GetDC)

SYMPTOM
  After `SetRoot` the very next call from Chromium's GPU process is
  `IDXGIFactory2::CreateSwapChainForComposition`, which was a stub (`fixme:dxgi:dxgi_factory_CreateSwapChainForComposition … stub!`);
  the GPU process then died and was relaunched six times and nothing was ever painted. With the swapchain provided,
  the page was still blank because `IDXGISurface1::GetDC` (used by Chromium's software compositor to rasterise the
  page into the swapchain back buffer) was a semi-stub: the GDI drawing never landed in the texture
  (`centre pixel 000000`).

WINDOWS BEHAVIOUR RESTORED
  A composition swapchain (no HWND) is created through the hidden-window path and its back buffers are GDI-capable;
  `GetDC`/`ReleaseDC` on a surface give a DC whose writes reach the underlying texture; and, after each present, the
  just-rendered buffer is composited into the window that dcomp registered as a composition target for the swapchain.

TEST
  Exercised end-to-end by the reproducer and by `dlls/dcomp/tests/dcomp.c`; no dxgi-only unit test yet (the dxgi
  suite has no composition coverage) — evidence is the trace (`Created composition swapchain … with hidden window`,
  `centre pixel d06020`, blit into the target window) and the reproducer's OCR.
